 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "roomba e5 wont charge properly, sometimes it does sometimes it doesnt"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Intermittent charging on a Roomba E5 is most commonly caused by dirty metal contacts on the robot or the base, which prevents a reliable connection. It could also be an issue with the power adapter or the wall socket itself. Please unplug the base, wipe the gold charging pins on both the base and the bottom of your Roomba with a dry cloth to remove any dust, then plug it into a different wall outlet if you can and leave it there for 30 minutes to see if the light stays solid amber."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Did the wipe. Contacts were dull with a greasy grey film and loads of hair on the robot ones. It's charged every night for 4 days now with no error. No hot or burning smell from it either."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That is excellent news. The greasy film and hair were most likely preventing a solid connection, which is very common on Roombas. To keep this up, I would suggest giving those charging contacts a quick wipe with a dry cloth once every couple of weeks to stop the buildup returning. If it starts acting up again in future, checking the socket and adapter first is also worth doing. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
